description:
Objective: under the protected profile, the VS Code extension applies the same runtime-selection rules as JetBrains:
- a strict, fail-closed profile read;
- installed-only daemon, proxy and wrapper selection;
- MOE_DAEMON_PATH, MOE_PROXY_PATH and MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1 (CQ-R13c1's marker) passed to agent launches;
- refusal instead of fallback.
This is CQ-R01 follow-up 7. JetBrains stays primary, so this row follows CQ-RF01..RF04 and CQ-R13c1, and mirrors their final behavior.

Created by architect-e4b7eee0 on 2026-10-30, when the human moved the non-gating R01 follow-ups out of CQ-R13.

Deliverable:
- The moe-vscode daemon spawn and agent launch paths implement the rules above under the protected profile.
- The legacy profile is unchanged.
- Add a unit test for the selection, and keep the startup regression tests passing.

Out of scope:
- JetBrains changes;
- persistent provenance for VS Code, unless CQ-RF01's store is shareable as-is (note it if so);
- .moe edits;
- enabling verified-local.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): cd moe-vscode && npm test && npm run compile
